overviewKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#main-window-overview\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":33113,"e":33194,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<img alt=\"korTTY main window\" src=\"../assets/screenshots/main/main-window.png\" />"]},{"s":33202,"e":33281,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<img alt=\"Main window layout\" src=\"../assets/diagrams/mainwindow-layout.svg\" />"]},{"s":33289,"e":33481,"k":"block","t":"A fresh korTTY window: the menu bar, the terminal area (where session tabs and the optional dashboard appear once you connect), and the status bar. The following diagram maps the same regions:","f":[]},{"s":33489,"e":33564,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<img alt=\"korTTY architecture\" src=\"../assets/diagrams/architecture.svg\" />"]},{"s":33572,"e":33611,"k":"block","t":"korTTY's main window has these regions:","f":[]},{"s":33625,"e":33976,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Menu barKTPH001 — File · Edit · Connections · Security · Configuration · Tools · Plugins · View · Teamwork · AI · Help. All features are reachable here and via KTPH002keyboard shortcutsKTPH003. A live KTPH004JobScheduler statusKTPH005 menu appears after KTPH006HelpKTPH007 when a scheduled entry is active.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<a href=\"../reference/keyboard-shortcuts.html\">","</a>","<strong>","</strong>","<em>","</em>"]},{"s":33986,"e":34752,"k":"block","t":"KTPH007Tab barKTPH008 — each SSH/Mosh session runs in its own tab. KTPH009KTPH000KTPH010+KTPH011KTPH001KTPH012 opens Quick Connect for a new tab; KTPH013KTPH002KTPH014+KTPH015KTPH003KTPH016 / KTPH017KTPH004KTPH018+KTPH019KTPH005KTPH020+KTPH021KTPH006KTPH022 switch tabs. With KTPH023Open tool windows as tabsKTPH024 enabled (KTPH025Window settingsKTPH026), management tools such as Snippets, the JobScheduler or the AI Manager open here as tabs too — in the window whose menu you used — instead of as separate windows.","f":["<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-t\">T</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-tab\">Tab</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-tab\">Tab</kbd>","<strong>","</strong>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","</span>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","</span>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>","<strong>","</strong>","<a href=\"../reference/settings/window.html\">","</a>"]},{"s":34762,"e":35093,"k":"block","t":"KTPH003DashboardKTPH004 (toggle KTPH005KTPH000KTPH006+KTPH007KTPH001KTPH008+KTPH009KTPH002KTPH010) — a side panel listing every open connection with status dots, protocol badges and AI-agent badges. See KTPH011DashboardKTPH012 below.","f":["<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-d\">D</kbd>","<strong>","</strong>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>","<a href=\"#dashboard\">","</a>"]},{"s":35103,"e":35474,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000File browserKTPH001 (KTPH002View → File Browser ▸ Show on Left / Show on RightKTPH003) — a dockable local file manager with navigation toolbar, path bar, filter, type icons and a folder/file/selection counter. Its side, width, hidden-file state and last directory are restored on the next launch. See KTPH004File browserKTPH005.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<a href=\"../features/file-browser.html\">","</a>"]},{"s":35484,"e":35585,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Terminal areaKTPH001 — the active terminal, with optional split-screen and broadcast input.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":35595,"e":35717,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Status barKTPH001 — connection state, host/IP, active protocol, temporary SSH-key timer and connection duration.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":35786,"e":35810,"k":"block","t":"Terminal-only fullscreen","f":[]},{"s":35818,"e":36631,"k":"block","t":"Press KTPH006KTPH000KTPH007+KTPH008KTPH001KTPH009+KTPH010KTPH002KTPH011 (or KTPH012View → Terminal-only FullscreenKTPH013) to show the whole korTTY window — menus, tabs and status bar included — kept at its previous window size and centered on an empty fullscreen background, so the desktop and other windows stop competing for attention. KTPH014View → Hide terminal scrollbars in fullscreenKTPH015 removes the scrollbars too. A transparent terminal background becomes opaque while fullscreen is active and returns to its saved level when you leave. Press KTPH016KTPH003KTPH017+KTPH018KTPH004KTPH019+KTPH020KTPH005KTPH021 again to restore.","f":["<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-f\">F</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-f\">F</kbd>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>"]},{"s":36662,"e":36744,"k":"block","t":"DashboardKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#dashboard\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":36753,"e":37079,"k":"block","t":"Toggle the dashboard with KTPH003KTPH000KTPH004+KTPH005KTPH001KTPH006+KTPH007KTPH002KTPH008 or KTPH009View → Show DashboardKTPH010. It slides in on the left, sizes its width to the longest entry, and follows the active App Design's colors.","f":["<kbd class=\"key-control\">Ctrl</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-shift\">Shift</kbd>","<kbd class=\"key-d\">D</kbd>","<span class=\"keys\">","<span>","</span>","<span>","</span>","</span>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":37087,"e":37307,"k":"block","t":"The header shows the panel title with two buttons: a collapse/expand toggle (collapses everything while any node is open, expands everything otherwise) and a refresh button. Below it, connections are organized as a tree:","f":[]},{"s":37321,"e":37402,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Main windowKTPH001 — the root node, with an active/total session count.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":37412,"e":37650,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000EnvironmentsKTPH001 — connections whose stored credential has an environment (for example KTPH002ProductionKTPH003 or KTPH004TestKTPH005) are clustered under an environment node; connections without one sit directly under the main window.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<em>","</em>","<em>","</em>"]},{"s":37660,"e":37832,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000GroupsKTPH001 — tabs assigned to a connection group appear under their group node. Saving a changed group in the Connection Manager updates open tabs immediately.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":37847,"e":38479,"k":"block","t":"Each connection row shows a type icon, a status dot, the server name, and a protocol badge (KTPH000, KTPH001 or KTPH002). The status dot distinguishes three states: filled green for a healthy connection, filled red for a connection that dropped unexpectedly (including a Mosh network interruption), and a hollow outline for a session that ended normally. Terminals with AI-agent runs carry the same ✋/⚡/⏸/✓ badge as elsewhere. Hovering a row shows KTPH003 and the connection state; double-click (or KTPH005KTPH004KTPH006) focuses the session's tab.","f":["<code>ssh</code>","<code>mosh</code>","<code>local</code>","<code>user@host</code>","<kbd class=\"key-enter\">Enter</kbd>","<span class=\"keys\">","</span>"]},{"s":38487,"e":38804,"k":"block","t":"Right-click a connection for KTPH000FocusKTPH001, KTPH002DuplicateKTPH003, KTPH004ReconnectKTPH005, KTPH006SFTP-Client...KTPH007 (connected sessions only) and KTPH008CloseKTPH009. A footer keeps a running \"connected of total\" count, and an empty panel shows a placeholder until the first session opens.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":38834,"e":38928,"k":"block","t":"macOS Dock menuKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#macos-dock-menu\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":38937,"e":391